# The Ledger | EXT | Townland Of Cloonagh | DAY | constance, mr_hartley | See what the column means | Bailiffs, a rope, a roof coming down. A woman sits on the ditch and says nothing. {constance} holds the list | | 6 | crowd=40, stunts=roof pulled down, animals=horses
# The Ledger | INT | Rent Office | NIGHT | constance | Forge mercy | The book is open at the next name. She dips the pen and writes "paid" | {constance} falsifies the rents | 4 | props=rent ledger
# The Ledger | INT | Dining Room | NIGHT | constance, mr_hartley, pym | Be audited | {pym} carves, praises the mutton and remarks on a curious pattern in October. The meat on the dish is green by the time he sets down the knife | The haunting comes indoors | 6 | vfx=food spoiling, props=dinner service+portable desk
# The House's Death | INT | Back Stair | NIGHT | constance, keener, brigid | See her face | A woman combing grey hair on the stair turns: {constance}, at sixty. {brigid}, behind her, says: she cries for the house, child. She always did | {constance} understands whose death it is | 5 | vfx=apparition
# The House's Death | EXT | Stable Yard And Gates | NIGHT | constance, brigid | Open everything | Keys in every lock. The stores, then the gates. A long silent line of people, carrying | The stores are given away | 6 | crowd=200, props=keys+grain sacks
# The House's Death | INT | Rent Office | DAWN | mr_hartley, pym, constance | Read the book | Her father at the desk, turning blank pages. {pym} closes his portable desk and orders the coach. On the road, two women do not look back | | 4 | props=blank ledger
review: authored | 2026-11-12 | written whole; drawn from the famine clearances and the bean si of Irish tradition, with invented people
